MehulK Workstation & Sonoma Suite (v18.0, MehulK Personal Edition)
==================================================================

By MehulK. Formerly "WACK Sonoma Live Lockscreen" (the UUID is unchanged, so
settings and the enabled list carry over). One GNOME Shell extension made by
MK Workstation from two others, plus MehulK's own modules (extension.js,
topbar.js, lockWidgets.js, desktop.js, media.js, power.js, preview.js):

  WACK Sonoma Lockscreen 2.2.0 (rinzler69-wastaken)
    https://github.com/rinzler69-wastaken/wack-sonoma-lockscreen
    GPL-3.0 (LICENSE.GPL-3.0): sonoma.js, src/,
    stylesheet.css, and its schema keys

  Live Lock Screen (nick-redwill)
    https://github.com/nick-redwill/LiveLockScreen
    AGPL-3.0 (LICENSE.AGPL-3.0): live.js, core/, helpers/, utils/,
    external/, enums.js, and its schema keys

  MK Workstation: extension.js (the glue: both parts started while locked,
  lock / unlock animations, dimming, clock styling, avatar / notification
  switches, the fingerprint hint), prefs.js (the four-page settings window),
  the MK schema keys, and these changes to Live Lock Screen: mpv always
  without audio (aid=no, ao=null), no audio volume setting.

GPL-3.0 section 13 allows combining GPL-3.0 code with AGPL-3.0 code; the
combined work is conveyed under AGPL-3.0, each part keeping its own notice.
Left out of WACK: its GDM (login screen) part (src/pro/, crossSessionManager.js)
and its own settings pages. Changed in WACK: its wallpaper-colour cache lives in
~/.cache/wack-sonoma-lockscreen (0700) instead of a world-writable /var/tmp/wack
shared with GDM, and it no longer sweeps /var/tmp (src/main/cacheDir.js). Its uuid
(wack-lockscreen-clock@...) is a separate extension.
